# Canvas Rendering

- `renderer.ts` is draw-only: receives `CanvasRenderingContext2D` + `GameState`, no mutations
- Scale canvas for device pixel ratio in the hook, not in the renderer
- All drawing happens in one `render()` call per frame
- React must not re-render the canvas each frame; the engine calls `render()` via rAF

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
export function render(ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D, state: GameState): void

// ❌ BAD — game logic in renderer
if (ball.x > paddle.x) { state.scores[0]++ }
```
